field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-c6cf6088-a7ab-5fa5-b537-1853d335b7b8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c6cf6088-a7ab-5fa5-b537-1853d335b7b8" "answer-19361797-c18f-5c79-a0bb-1599c95a5d3a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6cf6088-a7ab-5fa5-b537-1853d335b7b8" :answer/id #uuid "c6cf6088-a7ab-5fa5-b537-1853d335b7b8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-19361797-c18f-5c79-a0bb-1599c95a5d3a" :answer/id #uuid "19361797-c18f-5c79-a0bb-1599c95a5d3a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6b957da1-0df2-5626-98d6-1a7c5a3632dc" :question/id #uuid "6b957da1-0df2-5626-98d6-1a7c5a3632dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-342601" :question/problem "$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(x+2)^{3}+3, & x\\in [-2,0) \\\\ x+1, & x\\in [0,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above function $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [-2,2).$ Let $f(x)$ be the $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n| I. | $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| II. | $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| III. | ${lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| IV. | $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth and continuous on $R$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is $\\text{false}.$ The function $F(x)$ has a jump discontinuity at $x=0.$ Its graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/2d/2d30d760181c95dd0764b9959ca91febb34e94618bb147d8022dae5745c38a1a.png)\n\n- Statement II is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-2,2).$ It consists of two smooth pieces.\n\n- Statement III is $\\text{true}.$ Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}((x+2)^{3}+3)=(0)^{3}+3=3\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}(x+1)=2+1=3.\n$$\n\nSo, ${lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x).$\n\n- Statement IV is $\\text{false}$ since statement I is false.\n\n**Note:** The $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R$ has the graph shown below.\n\n![](images/fc/fcdf5654322a6deff9d7598590b4e0e1ace6150020b4944ad844976fb0f70230.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-08ecb117-6c45-5463-b318-8c285506eabc" "answer-field-60253eb4-3e5a-59a0-8c20-7c861c025f6e" "answer-field-4b521d38-d990-5b0d-80fe-d03ebd685a00" "answer-field-a102f1e0-40e5-5ef6-a7de-a0e753751c70"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-08ecb117-6c45-5463-b318-8c285506eabc" :answer-field/id #uuid "08ecb117-6c45-5463-b318-8c285506eabc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-113f0528-6296-5edc-a471-87b1ca2ca4b8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-113f0528-6296-5edc-a471-87b1ca2ca4b8" "answer-7686472d-41c3-5025-a423-4ae9721b5993"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-113f0528-6296-5edc-a471-87b1ca2ca4b8" :answer/id #uuid "113f0528-6296-5edc-a471-87b1ca2ca4b8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7686472d-41c3-5025-a423-4ae9721b5993" :answer/id #uuid "7686472d-41c3-5025-a423-4ae9721b5993" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-60253eb4-3e5a-59a0-8c20-7c861c025f6e" :answer-field/id #uuid "60253eb4-3e5a-59a0-8c20-7c861c025f6e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-a698678d-21d8-5a48-b894-3c49a5fac693" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1e34f35d-c327-5601-b6ee-eb5051e0fda7" "answer-a698678d-21d8-5a48-b894-3c49a5fac693"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1e34f35d-c327-5601-b6ee-eb5051e0fda7" :answer/id #uuid "1e34f35d-c327-5601-b6ee-eb5051e0fda7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a698678d-21d8-5a48-b894-3c49a5fac693" :answer/id #uuid "a698678d-21d8-5a48-b894-3c49a5fac693" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4b521d38-d990-5b0d-80fe-d03ebd685a00" :answer-field/id #uuid "4b521d38-d990-5b0d-80fe-d03ebd685a00" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-ce0e6216-87df-59a6-808e-871e310b9484" :answer-field/choices ["answer-76b55157-f226-54be-8fd3-e576ce7da945" "answer-ce0e6216-87df-59a6-808e-871e310b9484"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-76b55157-f226-54be-8fd3-e576ce7da945" :answer/id #uuid "76b55157-f226-54be-8fd3-e576ce7da945" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce0e6216-87df-59a6-808e-871e310b9484" :answer/id #uuid "ce0e6216-87df-59a6-808e-871e310b9484" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a102f1e0-40e5-5ef6-a7de-a0e753751c70" :answer-field/id #uuid "a102f1e0-40e5-5ef6-a7de-a0e753751c70" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-151f3b2c-1198-5804-bb25-a1fa989b21a3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-151f3b2c-1198-5804-bb25-a1fa989b21a3" "answer-64cf008c-66db-51cd-bdbe-6511859f628e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-151f3b2c-1198-5804-bb25-a1fa989b21a3" :answer/id #uuid "151f3b2c-1198-5804-bb25-a1fa989b21a3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-64cf008c-66db-51cd-bdbe-6511859f628e" :answer/id #uuid "64cf008c-66db-51cd-bdbe-6511859f628e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-46096919-32d4-552d-ad62-e0e1723dd83b" :question/id #uuid "46096919-32d4-552d-ad62-e0e1723dd83b" :question/math-academy-id "q-342245" :question/problem "$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-4x, & x\\in [-2,0) \\\\ {x}^{3}, & x\\in [0,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above function $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [-2,2).$ Let $f(x)$ be the $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n| I. | $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| II. | $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| III. | ${lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| IV. | $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth and continuous on $R$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-2,2).$ Its graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/0a/0a29065f008fac7d3fd32d52b2ddc0b7d9360ffd75475f6c169eeb26582d22d2.png)\n\n- Statement II is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-2,2).$ It consists of two smooth pieces.\n\n- Statement III is $\\text{true}.$ Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}-4x=-4(-2)=8\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}{x}^{3}=(2)^{3}=8.\n$$\n\nSo, ${lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x).$\n\n- Statement IV is $\\text{true}$ since statements I, II, and III are all true.\n\n**Note:** The $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R$ has the graph shown below.\n\n![](images/d7/d750ad2f9ea2a85446b94f7b19009ef74eeea25b4ccd1bf8ff4f408a5df381e2.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-43f4ed93-3433-5da6-8034-8da63e770508" "answer-field-b9d9c24a-7b11-59ec-a4a0-6136392a9411" "answer-field-02397001-5967-5501-a894-ba22a52ed078" "answer-field-f6c6d28a-a8a0-5b03-a2be-c422eefbc276"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-43f4ed93-3433-5da6-8034-8da63e770508" :answer-field/id #uuid "43f4ed93-3433-5da6-8034-8da63e770508" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-4eb5b194-82d3-514f-a7ba-8de2203f7d4f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a0bab576-a7aa-5d44-bb81-8dddab1acc90" "answer-4eb5b194-82d3-514f-a7ba-8de2203f7d4f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a0bab576-a7aa-5d44-bb81-8dddab1acc90" :answer/id #uuid "a0bab576-a7aa-5d44-bb81-8dddab1acc90" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4eb5b194-82d3-514f-a7ba-8de2203f7d4f" :answer/id #uuid "4eb5b194-82d3-514f-a7ba-8de2203f7d4f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b9d9c24a-7b11-59ec-a4a0-6136392a9411" :answer-field/id #uuid "b9d9c24a-7b11-59ec-a4a0-6136392a9411" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-134b90c6-da6f-564c-b88c-9cde9a9b37af" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7aa2deb5-9607-580c-9d2a-b98702d2433d" "answer-134b90c6-da6f-564c-b88c-9cde9a9b37af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7aa2deb5-9607-580c-9d2a-b98702d2433d" :answer/id #uuid "7aa2deb5-9607-580c-9d2a-b98702d2433d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-134b90c6-da6f-564c-b88c-9cde9a9b37af" :answer/id #uuid "134b90c6-da6f-564c-b88c-9cde9a9b37af" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-02397001-5967-5501-a894-ba22a52ed078" :answer-field/id #uuid "02397001-5967-5501-a894-ba22a52ed078" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-1124e7b9-2d5f-5e41-894c-4012a241cbb4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fc0eac61-78a6-5e61-9741-36c63bed5514" "answer-1124e7b9-2d5f-5e41-894c-4012a241cbb4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc0eac61-78a6-5e61-9741-36c63bed5514" :answer/id #uuid "fc0eac61-78a6-5e61-9741-36c63bed5514" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1124e7b9-2d5f-5e41-894c-4012a241cbb4" :answer/id #uuid "1124e7b9-2d5f-5e41-894c-4012a241cbb4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f6c6d28a-a8a0-5b03-a2be-c422eefbc276" :answer-field/id #uuid "f6c6d28a-a8a0-5b03-a2be-c422eefbc276" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-930eef55-0159-5954-a696-d7ed742b7ec6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f8fa35e0-047b-50a2-976e-7044fdf2253d" "answer-930eef55-0159-5954-a696-d7ed742b7ec6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f8fa35e0-047b-50a2-976e-7044fdf2253d" :answer/id #uuid "f8fa35e0-047b-50a2-976e-7044fdf2253d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-930eef55-0159-5954-a696-d7ed742b7ec6" :answer/id #uuid "930eef55-0159-5954-a696-d7ed742b7ec6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3df34aa2-66f8-53fb-b84c-e23ff9464f43" :question/id #uuid "3df34aa2-66f8-53fb-b84c-e23ff9464f43" :question/math-academy-id "q-342264" :question/problem "$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x, & x\\in [-2,0) \\\\ 3, & x\\in [0,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above function $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [-2,2).$ Let $f(x)$ be the $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n| I. | $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| II. | $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| III. | ${lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| IV. | $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth and continuous on $R$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is $\\text{false}.$ The function $F(x)$ has a jump discontinuity at $x=0.$ Its graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/7a/7afa339233c7e21eda233f5b67ccf8be9e05fb4ce9484c98eaf59eb790e651ab.png)\n\n- Statement II is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-2,2).$ It consists of two smooth pieces.\n\n- Statement III is $\\text{false}.$ Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}x=-2\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}3=3.\n$$\n\nSo, ${lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)\\ne {lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x).$\n\n- Statement IV is $\\text{false}$ since statements I and III are false.\n\n**Note:** The $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R$ has the graph shown below.\n\n![](images/1a/1ac6956ec22cfed2d304cc5c2352cf1fdf4c795ea423e7a19c8e3a3e2dc843ed.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bc32ec31-8aab-5e25-95f6-47aed03f7c3b" "answer-field-0a027e30-e5db-5ef5-823b-5d5213ffe1be" "answer-field-0515496f-04cd-566b-90f7-87a3f4b76092" "answer-field-8b781fbf-b13f-5c71-940f-e7a40eb71a60"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bc32ec31-8aab-5e25-95f6-47aed03f7c3b" :answer-field/id #uuid "bc32ec31-8aab-5e25-95f6-47aed03f7c3b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-c442eea8-eb9b-51fe-9d23-75ab92b8ffe1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c442eea8-eb9b-51fe-9d23-75ab92b8ffe1" "answer-f9060f67-f7b4-5a5d-bfd7-7abf56ccf59e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c442eea8-eb9b-51fe-9d23-75ab92b8ffe1" :answer/id #uuid "c442eea8-eb9b-51fe-9d23-75ab92b8ffe1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f9060f67-f7b4-5a5d-bfd7-7abf56ccf59e" :answer/id #uuid "f9060f67-f7b4-5a5d-bfd7-7abf56ccf59e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0a027e30-e5db-5ef5-823b-5d5213ffe1be" :answer-field/id #uuid "0a027e30-e5db-5ef5-823b-5d5213ffe1be" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-c884611a-198a-588d-a475-eb02622d1e56" :answer-field/choices ["answer-057eb7f3-190a-5da9-a784-33d6a0e88a3a" "answer-c884611a-198a-588d-a475-eb02622d1e56"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-057eb7f3-190a-5da9-a784-33d6a0e88a3a" :answer/id #uuid "057eb7f3-190a-5da9-a784-33d6a0e88a3a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c884611a-198a-588d-a475-eb02622d1e56" :answer/id #uuid "c884611a-198a-588d-a475-eb02622d1e56" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0515496f-04cd-566b-90f7-87a3f4b76092" :answer-field/id #uuid "0515496f-04cd-566b-90f7-87a3f4b76092" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-15b4446a-3837-52de-923e-6861cab63dfa" :answer-field/choices ["answer-15b4446a-3837-52de-923e-6861cab63dfa" "answer-0bdf9085-5e57-5fef-9288-dd2d5b77cfd5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-15b4446a-3837-52de-923e-6861cab63dfa" :answer/id #uuid "15b4446a-3837-52de-923e-6861cab63dfa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0bdf9085-5e57-5fef-9288-dd2d5b77cfd5" :answer/id #uuid "0bdf9085-5e57-5fef-9288-dd2d5b77cfd5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8b781fbf-b13f-5c71-940f-e7a40eb71a60" :answer-field/id #uuid "8b781fbf-b13f-5c71-940f-e7a40eb71a60" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-2beb1cb1-5d44-5f64-aa49-099923f8b16b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2beb1cb1-5d44-5f64-aa49-099923f8b16b" "answer-ec2972fd-47e3-5529-9b6d-d5a3d01b3766"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2beb1cb1-5d44-5f64-aa49-099923f8b16b" :answer/id #uuid "2beb1cb1-5d44-5f64-aa49-099923f8b16b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ec2972fd-47e3-5529-9b6d-d5a3d01b3766" :answer/id #uuid "ec2972fd-47e3-5529-9b6d-d5a3d01b3766" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186317343 :question/problem "$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+1, & x\\in [-3,0] \\\\ \\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}, & x\\in (0,3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above function $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [-3,3).$ Let $f(x)$ be the $6$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n| I. | $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-3,3)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| II. | $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-3,3)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| III. | ${lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}F(x)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| IV. | $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth and continuous on $R$ | {{field-4}} |" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186316829 :answer-field/correct 17592186315462 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186316982 :answer-field/correct 17592186315923 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186316971 :answer-field/correct 17592186316463 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186316679 :answer-field/correct 17592186316307 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-fa5cac21-63bb-59e7-aa34-0b7a399b8755" :question/id #uuid "fa5cac21-63bb-59e7-aa34-0b7a399b8755" :question/math-academy-id "q-343062" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $8$-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+4$ defined on $[-4,4).$  Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of the Fourier series of the $8$-periodic extension of $G(x)=x$ from the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$\n\nThe Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+4∼\\frac{20}{3}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{32(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is  \n{{field-2}}\nand  \n{{field-3}}\non $R,$ we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\nx∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-4}}\\cdot {{field-5}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $F(x)$ is an even function. So, the Fourier series of its $2L$-periodic extension has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}cos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=4.$ Thus, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{20}{3}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{32(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}cos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{4}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that  \n\n- the function $F$ is continuously differentiable on $(-4,4),$\n\n- continuous on $[-4,4),$ and\n\n- satisfies $F(-4)=F(4),$ if we extend the value at $x=4$ using the formula $F(x)=\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+4.$\n\nTherefore, the $8$-periodic extension $f$ is\n$\\text{continuous}$ and\n$\\text{piecewise smooth}$\non $R,$ so we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}\\,(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+4) & ∼\\frac{d}{dx}\\,(\\frac{20}{3})+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{d}{dx}(\\frac{32(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}cos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{4})) \\\\ x & ∼0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{32(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}(-\\frac{n\\pi }{4}sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{4})) \\\\ x & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{-8(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{4}) \\\\ x & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{8(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\cdot sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{4}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6cca0358-5b5c-5eb3-a2c2-97ae199a0d9a" "answer-field-e4d884b0-d058-5f44-82e3-a0072396491a" "answer-field-5c580a2d-1eaf-59df-bd57-50b95a0b8b16" "answer-field-04f21919-6b70-5a22-9660-a18b41b9f85b" "answer-field-42cacff0-1789-5047-806f-1ce56c82fffe"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6cca0358-5b5c-5eb3-a2c2-97ae199a0d9a" :answer-field/id #uuid "6cca0358-5b5c-5eb3-a2c2-97ae199a0d9a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-af38a2c